$, and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33534e52-22a6-53b6-ab24-f2fc95901ef6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508273} {:answer/id #uuid "7d632778-d7d0-5b8e-8054-b8393a63d67d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508316} {:answer/id #uuid "bac5aab2-c0b2-503d-8b54-7be5dbbb5e27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508340} {:answer/id #uuid "f826503c-35ad-5dec-94b5-1a3ecf16f589" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508372}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bac5aab2-c0b2-503d-8b54-7be5dbbb5e27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508340} :answer-field/id #uuid "03b806d6-996d-59c5-bbcd-324cbd1e9495" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508242} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f2c2bcf-334b-56b0-a302-17ebf4f4cff4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508251} {:answer/id #uuid "53b071d1-754c-5b35-a614-05465b4639f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "53b071d1-754c-5b35-a614-05465b4639f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508294} :answer-field/id #uuid "760e3944-245b-5965-ab85-16e5a3fc8a38" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508315}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "88d9972c-3f5b-5e57-9021-7026fbb79903" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}10a + 3b &=-1 \\\\ 9a + 18b &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $3$, while in the second equation it is $18$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-6}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $-18$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $18$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}&(10a + 3b = -1)\\cdot (-6) \\\\ &9a + 18b = -5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-60a - 18b &= 6 \\\\\n9a + 18b &= -5 \\\\\n(-60a + 9a) &= (6 - 5) \\\\\n-51a &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-6}$, and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Vari