e the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-15$, while in the second equation it is $-3$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by ${\\color{blue}-5}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $15$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-15$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}&-5a - 15b = 8 \\\\ &(-8a - 3b = 10)\\cdot (-5)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-5a - 15b &= 8 \\\\\n40a + 15b &= -50 \\\\\n(-5a + 40a) &= (8 - 50) \\\\\n35a &= -42\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{second}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-5}$, and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508342 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "220d1f0d-705a-51be-82e7-454a15c207cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508263} {:answer/id #uuid "46b40b50-8f41-5621-8507-c13a24eb8d3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508284} {:answer/id #uuid "9de0642e-8140-505e-bfef-fd699ee965c9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 175