ce that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $3$, while in the second equation it is $9$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-3}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $-9$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $9$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}&(10a + 3b = -1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\ &9a + 9b = -5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-30a - 9b &= 3 \\\\\n9a + 9b &= -5 \\\\\n(-30a + 9a) &= (3 - 5) \\\\\n-21a &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-3}$, and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508345 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "19abff8d-ae9e-5607-a20e-fabfdd36db34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508258} {:answer/id #uuid "20a941f3-cb0b-5f69-ab43-56c13080d620" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508261} {:answer/id #uuid "46814826-f010-593a-b3e8-5f63f785645f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508282} {:answer/id #uuid "5594cdc5-034f-5627-abd8-dfbefb4c1912" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508296}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4681482