of $-24$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}&(-8a + 4b = 5)\\cdot (6) \\\\ &-2a - 24b = 5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-48a + 24b &= 30 \\\\\n-2a - 24b &= 5 \\\\\n(-48a - 2a) &= (30 + 5) \\\\\n-50a &= 35\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}6}$, and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3329bb61-ee30-5582-b95e-93e49d25acbb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508272} {:answer/id #uuid "5745dbcd-d2ec-538d-a5c0-6e40a55ff9c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508297}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5745dbcd-d2ec-538d-a5c0-6e40a55ff9c3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508297} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b6e85c3-b039-528d-a630-269f4ab66bb7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508309} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7589e36d-b3bd-5962-bc29-ef4192f475f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508313} {:answer/id #uuid "c7eecde