 18 \\\\\n-7a - 3b &= 9 \\\\\n(-3a - 7a) &= (18 + 9) \\\\\n-10a &= 27\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-3}$, and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508354 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "39a6814c-18ed-51c5-ac72-0b9e8d2d7b22" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "second" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508276} {:answer/id #uuid "b370d6a5-ae0f-513a-be14-2ead2c5dd0ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508338}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b370d6a5-ae0f-513a-be14-2ead2c5dd0ee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "first" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508338} :answer-field/id #uuid "15446ed6-06ee-5e8f-b9db-fb23758c2828" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508257} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e3b6170-053d-5e20-bf03-eb7b7f0b9b9f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508271} {:answer/id #uuid "34c59b71-7028-5a50-90c2-416e17328ce0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508274} {:answer/id #uuid "898c0b7e-ab07-55a0-9d3e-8d2228d97878" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 1759218604