1-9e0a-80d446b48de7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494 :db/ident :answer-field.type/select} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186508301}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e58c3e5b-b391-5afd-9ee6-da3df80ea5cd" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}a - 3b &=-6 \\\\ -7a - 6b &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-3$, while in the second equation it is $-6$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-2}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $6$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-6$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}&(a - 3b = -6)\\cdot (-2) \\\\ &-7a - 6b = 9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2a + 6b &= 12 \\\\\n-7a - 6b &= 9 \\\\\n(-2a - 7a) &= (12 + 9) \\\\\n-9a &= 21\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-2}$, and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186508370 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e7bfcbe-4913-53e0-98c7-171965adfe62" :knowledge-point/title "Eliminating the Second Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2830d30e-f96c