iculty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f40ec0f3-3ce5-52b3-a3e7-9ca324b7f03c" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5a - 4b &=6 \\\\ 8a - 12b &=-6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $b$ from the system:\nUse an integer multiplier and leave the other equation unchanged.\n\nTo eliminate $b$, multiply the\n{{field-1}}\nequation by\n{{field-2}},\nand add the equations." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $b$ in the first equation is $-4$, while in the second equation it is $-12$.\n\nIf we multiply the first equation by ${\\color{blue}-3}$, then the coefficient of $b$ will turn into $12$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-12$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}&(5a - 4b = 6)\\cdot (-3) \\\\ &8a - 12b = -6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $b$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-15a + 12b &= -18 \\\\\n8a - 12b &= -6 \\\\\n(-15a + 8a) &= (-18 - 6) \\\\\n-7a &= -24\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n> *To eliminate $b$, multiply the $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\text{first}}$ equation by $\\bbox[3pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}-3}$, and add the equations*."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186509050 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192656 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "2dbf4e1a-2c87-562d-8c4d-41fd32e79b86" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a System of Equations by Eliminating the First Variable" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050190 :topic/title "Solving Systems of Linear Equations Using Elimination: One Transformation"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b5ee4058-4cb0-5815-af4f-31cb5f7f4b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b5ee4058-4cb0-5815-af4f-31cb5f7f4b9e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509104} :answer-field/id #uuid "491f86ca-62f3-5ea9-8428-178689de26c2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509073} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "accbd167-8445-5f77-b722-a480de8d9a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "accbd167-8445-5f77-b722-a480de8d9a7d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509102} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0ddcf7e-8326-53ea-93be-7d843009b320" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186509096}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "02c41293-f116-502f-be60-22954dd650e1" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations:\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-8x + 5y &=1 \\\\ -2x - 7y &=25\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the solution $(x, y)$ to this system by eliminating the variable $x$.\n\nThe solution is $($\n{{field-1}}\n$,$\n{{field-2}}\n$)$." :question/worked-solution "Notice that the coefficient of $x$ in the first equation is $-8$, while in the second equation it is $-2$.\n\nIf we multiply the second equation by $-4$, then the $x$-coefficient will become $8$, which will cancel with the coefficient of $-8$ in the first equation.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}&-8x + 5y = 1 \\\\ &(-2x - 7y = 25) \\cdot (-4)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $x$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-8x + 5y &= 1 \\\\\n8x + 28y &= -100 \\\\\n(5y + 28y) &= (1 - 100) \\\\\n33y &= -99 \\\\\ny &= -3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solution must have $y = -3$. However, we still need to find $x$. To do this, we substitute $y = -3$ back into one of the equations. Let's choose the second equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n-2x - 7y &= 25 \\\\\n-2x - 7(-3) &= 25 \\\\\n-2x + 21 &= 25 \\\\\n-2x &= 4 \\\\\nx &= -2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the system of equations is $x=-2, \\,y=-3$, which can be expressed as $(-2,-3)$."}]}
